{"agent":"lean1-schema-trim","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The comment above this line claims the assertion verifies \"the add tools still carry the answer arguments,\" but `ADD_TOOLS` is a module-level constant that is non-empty in any import of `mcp.py`, so `assert ADD_TOOLS` is unconditionally true and can never fail. Nothing in either ratchet test actually verifies that `relation`/`check_only` are still present on the add tools: the loop above only flags a description that is *present and longer than 200 chars*, so if a regression dropped `relation` or `check_only` from every entry of `ADD_TOOLS` (or from `_properties` where they are injected), `long_ones` stays empty, `assert not long_ones` passes, and `assert ADD_TOOLS` also passes. The intended guard — e.g. `assert all(arg in _schema(spec)[\"properties\"] for spec in ADD_TOOLS.values() for arg in (\"relation\", \"check_only\"))` — is missing, so the test silently green-lights exactly the deletion it was written to prevent.","digest":"366cda43c887a221","location":"tests/test_mcp_tool_budget.py:41 (`assert ADD_TOOLS` in test_shared_parameter_descriptions_are_not_repeated_in_full)","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_mcp_tool_budget.py:41 (`assert ADD_TOOLS` in test_shared_parameter_descriptions_are_not_repeated_in_full)"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":6800,"diff_sha":"a36b746fdf9f68eb125aa9aa9db3cbebdec6fc02c20715607f6385ab87c0b925","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-mcp-schema-trim","elapsed_s":134.4,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["tests/test_mcp_tool_budget.py:41 (`assert ADD_TOOLS` in test_shared_parameter_descriptions_are_not_repeated_in_full)"],"unreviewed":[]},